      "writtenOn": "2019-06-26T19:11:40Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "My first thought for how to do something more unified would be to have IOEX() in gpio.inc add an entry into \"struct gpio_info gpio_list[]\", storing the ioex_port in a new field added to struct gpio_info.\n\nUnfortunately, the implementation of gpio_set/get_level() etc is spread among chip/*/gpio.c so all of those would need to be touched to add handling for the new IOEX signals. Maybe all those API functions should move up to common/gpio.c and then call down into either a per-chip driver (for GPIO signals) or the ioexpander_drv (for IOEX signals).",
      "parentUuid": "1e1cf9f8_4dde34b6",
